1‚¤textÙ'And they are the thousands of Manasseh.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤text·And of Zebulun he said,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#Rejoice, Zebulun, in thy going out;¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¼And, Issachar, in thy tents.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ-They shall call the people unto the mountain;¦layout ‚¤textÙ3There they shall offer sacrifices of righteousness:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ1For they shall suck of the abundance of the seas,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ!And of treasures hid in the sand.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines”‚¤text³And of Gad he said,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!Blessed be he that enlargeth Gad:¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¶He dwelleth as a lion,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ/And teareth the arm with the crown of the head.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines•‚¤textÙ+And he provided the first part for himself,¦layout ‚¤textÙ;Because there, in a portion of the lawgiver, was he seated;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ)And he came with the heads of the people,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ$He executed the justice of the LORD,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¾And his judgments with Israel.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤text³And of Dan he said,¦layout ‚¤text¶Dan is a lion's whelp:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textºHe shall leap from Bashan.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines”‚¤text¸And of Naphtali he said,¦layout ‚¤textÙ"O Naphtali, satisfied with favour,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ'And full with the blessing of the LORD:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ$Possess thou the west and the south.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines”‚¤textµAnd of Asher he said,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#Let Asher be blessed with children;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ&Let him be acceptable to his brethren,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ And let him dip his foot in oil.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Thy shoes shall be iron and brass;¦layout ‚¤textÙ*And as thy days, so shall thy strength be.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ,There is none like unto the God of Jeshurun,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'Who rideth upon the heaven in thy help,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ!And in his excellency on the sky.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤text¾The eternal God is thy refuge,¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And underneath are the everlasting arms:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ3And he shall thrust out the enemy from before thee;¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¼And shall say, Destroy them.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ(Israel then shall dwell in safety alone:¦layout ‚¤textµThe fountain of Jacob¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ&Shall be upon a land of corn and wine;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ%Also his heavens shall drop down dew.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines–‚¤text¹Happy art thou, O Israel:¦layout ‚¤textÙ2Who is like unto thee, O people saved by the LORD,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text·The shield of thy help,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ'And who is the sword of thy excellency!¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ1And thine enemies shall be found liars unto thee;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ,And thou shalt tread upon their high places.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse